      "description": "Watch Olympiakos Piraeus vs Jagiellonia Białystok highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 16, 2026. The UEFA Europa League returned with intensity as Olympiakos Piraeus welcomed Jagiellonia Białystok to their home turf on September 16, 2026. This opening fixture promised a clash of styles as the Greek giants aimed to make a statement against their Polish opponents. A Tense Opening Half The match ignited in the 20th minute when the visitors struck first. Nik Prelec turned provider, setting up Kajetan Szmyt , who clinical finish gave Jagiellonia Białystok a surprising early lead. The goal sparked a physical response from both sides, with the referee busy issuing yellow cards to Norbert Wojtuszek and Bruno Onyemaechi as the Polish side fought to maintain their advantage. However, Olympiakos found their rhythm late in the half. In the 43rd minute, Panagiotis Retsos delivered a pinpoint assist for Armando Gonzalez , who made no mistake in front of goal to level the score. The teams headed into the break with everything still to play for after a high-octane 45 minutes. Yaremchuk Secures the Points The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to find a breakthrough. Olympiakos introduced Roman Yaremchuk in the 62nd minute, a substitution that would prove vital. As the clock ticked down, the game became increasingly fractious, with Santiago Hezze and Bernardo Vital entering the referee's book amidst a flurry of tactical changes from both camps. The decisive moment arrived in the 84th minute. Remo Freuler showcased his vision with a brilliant pass to find Roman Yaremchuk , who slotted the ball home to complete the comeback. Despite late pressure and further substitutions from Jagiellonia , the home side held firm through four minutes of stoppage time to secure a hard-fought victory."
